WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.548 --> 00:00:02.090
RETO MEIER: Today
we're talking about

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.270
industry-leading security, AI
solutions, study materials,

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.230
and science.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.930
I'm Reto, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.540
you the lowest-latency news.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.310
At Google Cloud,
we defend your data

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.170
against threats and
fraudulent activity

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.990
using the same infrastructure
and security services

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.510
we use for our own operations.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.010
Our goal is to be the
most effective partner

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.880
as you transform your
business for a digital world,

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.430
whether your system's running
Google Cloud, in other clouds,

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.930
or on-prem.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.750
Our trusted cloud enables
your digital transformation

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.930
while also supporting your
security transformation.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.900
Check out the post for specifics
of our three new trusted cloud

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.790
requirements-- a
secure platform that

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.060
delivers transparency and
enables sovereignty, a proven

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.580
zero-trust architecture,
and shared fate,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.280
not shared responsibility.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.440
Google Cloud offers
lots of products

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.050
to support a wide
variety of use cases.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.000
But how do you even
know where to start?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.590
Don't worry, we've
got you covered.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.650
The "4 Words or Less"
Google Cloud developers

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.660
cheat sheet describes
each Google Cloud

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.825
product in four words or less.

00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:07.700
If you're just getting
started, this resource

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.500
gives you a quick
overview of all

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.263
that's available to
you on Google Cloud.

00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:12.680
And if you're more
experienced, it

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.990
can be a great way to
identify new products that you

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.390
might want learn more about.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.520
Download the PDF of
the latest version

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.820
at the links in the
description or on GitHub.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.550
Gartner has named Google
a leader in its 2021

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.640
Magic Quadrant for Cloud
AI developer services.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.490
We believe this recognition is
based on Gartner's evaluation

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.410
of Google Cloud's
language, vision,

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:36.440
conversational and structured
data services and solutions

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.820
for developers.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.340
This recognition is also a
reflection of the confidence

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.550
and satisfaction that
customers have in our products,

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.920
from a cohesive AI
stack for developers

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.100
to purpose-built AI solutions
for industry use cases.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.970
Check out the blog post for
more of what Gartner has to say.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.860
Drawing on the experience
of our customers,

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.690
the Google Cloud
Born-Digital Summit

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:58.700
will offer practical
guidance on building

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.790
a resilient and scalable
foundation for great customer

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.140
experiences.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.970
Over this half-day
event, we'll highlight

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.700
proven best-practice approaches
to data, architecture,

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.250
diversity, and
inclusion and growth

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.320
with Google Cloud solutions.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.270
Born-Digital is an event
for app developers,

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.100
technology innovators,
and business leaders

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.665
who are disrupting the market
and shaping the future.

00:02:18.665 --> 00:02:20.540
Check out the post to
register and learn more

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.137
about the March 25 event.

00:02:23.137 --> 00:02:25.220
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.900
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.060
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.170
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.120
We'll see you in the cloud.

